# 18. Read Optimization Summary

Workflow minimizes Firestore reads by:

- Using one Users collection
- Embedding assignment data
- Embedding proof data
- Embedding timeline
- Embedding recommendation summary
- Embedding incident summary
- Using lightweight dashboard statistics
- Avoiding unnecessary collections

This design keeps the MVP simple while remaining scalable for future enhancements.
# 19. Firestore Query Strategy

The database should be queried efficiently to minimize Firestore reads and improve application performance.

Queries should always retrieve only the data required by the current screen.

Avoid downloading unnecessary documents.

---

# 19.1 Dashboard Queries

Dashboard should load using lightweight queries.

Recommended reads:

- Organization document (dashboardStats)
- Recent tasks (limited)
- Recent notifications (limited)

Dashboard should never load every task or employee.

---

# 19.2 Employee Queries

Managers view only active employees within their organization.

Example filters:

```text
organizationId == currentOrganization
role == employee
isActive == true
```

Optional sorting:

```text
availability
name
activeTaskCount
```

---

# 19.3 Task Queries

Task List

```text
organizationId == currentOrganization
isActive == true
```

Optional filters

- Status
- Priority
- Assigned Employee
- Due Date

Use Firestore queries instead of filtering in React whenever possible.

---

# 19.4 Recommendation Queries

Recommendations are only loaded when:

- Opening Task Details
- Viewing recommendation history
- Evaluation module

Task List should use the embedded recommendationSummary instead.

---

# 19.5 Incident Queries

Managers should query:

```text
organizationId
status == open
```

Task Details should use the embedded incidentSummary unless full incident details are requested.

---

# 19.6 Notification Queries

Load only notifications belonging to the current user.

Example:

```text
recipientUserId == currentUser
```

Order by:

```text
createdAt DESC
```

Limit:

```text
20
```

Older notifications may be loaded on demand.

---

# 19.7 Audit Log Queries

Audit logs should support filtering by:

- User
- Action
- Entity
- Date

Default sort:

```text
timestamp DESC
```

Audit logs should be paginated.

