# 21. Security Strategy

Security is enforced through Firebase Authentication and Firestore Security Rules.

Every request must satisfy all of the following:

- User is authenticated
- User belongs to the organization
- User has sufficient role permissions

---

## Admin

Can access:

- Organization
- Users
- Tasks
- Recommendations
- Incidents
- Notifications
- Audit Logs

---

## Manager

Can access:

- Employees
- Tasks
- Recommendations
- Incidents
- Notifications

Cannot:

- Manage organization
- Manage users
- View audit logs

---

## Employee

Can access:

- Own profile
- Assigned tasks
- Own notifications

Can update:

- Assigned task status
- Proof uploads

Cannot:

- View other employees
- Create tasks
- Generate recommendations
- Access audit logs

---

# 22. Soft Delete Strategy

Workflow uses soft deletion instead of permanently deleting business records.

Instead of deleting:

```text
DELETE task
```

The system updates:

```text
isActive = false
```

Benefits

- Audit history preserved
- References remain valid
- Data recovery possible
- Better enterprise practice

Applies to:

- Users
- Tasks
- Incidents
- Organizations (future)

Audit Logs should never be deleted.

Notifications may optionally be archived in future versions.

